post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> pi-ext-hindsight installed to /usr/share/pi/extensions/hindsight/

To make it available to pi, symlink it into the extensions directory:

    ln -s /usr/share/pi/extensions/hindsight ~/.pi/agent/extensions-ordered/00-hindsight

For the hindsight-coding-agent SKILL to be discoverable, link it into a skills root:

    ln -sfn /usr/share/pi/extensions/hindsight/skill ~/.pi/agent/skills/hindsight-coding-agent

Then create the config -- nothing is remembered until it exists:

    mkdir -p ~/.hindsight
    cp /usr/share/pi-ext-hindsight/coding-agent.json.example ~/.hindsight/coding-agent.json

Edit apiUrl to point at your Hindsight server (default in the example is
http://127.0.0.1:8889), set optInPaths, and leave autoUpdate false: this copy is
managed by pacman, and the adapter detects that and refuses to update itself.

The Hindsight server itself is a separate package (hindsight-api). Memory is off
for every project until a path appears in optInPaths.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
